---
// Literal recreation of the Claude Design canvas's Admin Dashboard screen
// (project/Admin.dc.html / AdminDark.dc.html -> NavSidebar role="admin" +
// this artboard's own inline top bar, extracted as AdminNavTop.astro) —
// this REPLACES the old AppShell/DESIGN.md admin dashboard that used to
// live at this same route (/admin, unchanged). Own dedicated shell, not
// Sales'/Inventory Staff's NavTop — the Admin artboard's own header
// (search width, breadcrumb, +New/Export placement) genuinely differs, per
// your explicit "do not assume the Admin shell should be identical"
// instruction; only NavSidebar.astro is shared (role="admin" branch added
// there, see that file's own header comment), since the design's own
// NavSidebar.dc.html source confirms Admin uses the exact same sidebar
// component, just a different role config.
//
// PERMISSIONS: unchanged — /admin is already gated to admin/super_admin by
// src/middleware.ts (ROLE_GATED_PREFIXES, from lib/roles.ts), not touched
// this turn. admin and super_admin share this identical dashboard (see
// ROLE_DASHBOARD) — no new role, no widened access for any other role.
//
// NO-FABRICATION DECISIONS — every KPI/chart/table value below is real,
// computed from existing tables/views/RPCs already used elsewhere in this
// project (dashboard_revenue_trend, inventory_value_summary, orders,
// support_tickets, inventory, products, profiles — zero new RPCs/views/
// migrations). Where the design shows a number/concept this schema
// genuinely has no equivalent for, it is either honestly omitted or
// relabeled to what it actually is — never copied from the demo, never
// silently reinterpreted:
//  - "Revenue this month" / "▲ 8.2% vs Aug" / sparkline: real IST
//    calendar-month-to-date revenue (dashboard_revenue_trend RPC, same
//    real function every other dashboard uses — excludes cancelled orders,
//    same as everywhere else). The month-over-month % is real when last
//    month had any revenue to compare against; the live data right now
//    has zero orders in August, so an honest "No orders last month" is
//    shown instead of a divide-by-zero/fabricated percentage. The
//    sparkline is a real inline SVG polyline over this month's actual
//    per-day revenue points (only rendered once ≥2 real days of data
//    exist — a single point can't form a line, and a flat placeholder
//    line would misrepresent "no trend yet" as "flat revenue").
//  - "Open orders" / "46 orders" / "12 to ship this week": real count +
//    real total value of orders in pending/confirmed/processing/shipped
//    (i.e. not yet delivered, and not cancelled/refunded) — labeled
//    honestly as exactly that set, not "to ship". "12 to ship this week"
//    has no real equivalent (no expected-ship-date field exists anywhere
//    in this schema) — replaced with a real per-status breakdown instead
//    (e.g. "3 pending · 1 processing"), which is genuinely more
//    informative and, unlike the demo line, entirely real.
//  - "Inventory value" / "3,418 SKUs · 4 categories": real
//    inventory_value_summary.inventory_value (retail price × on-hand,
//    active products only — same view Phase 8 already built), real active
//    product count, real category count.
//  - "Low-stock items" / "17" / "4 out of stock · 3 restocks due": real
//    count of active products with quantity_on_hand <= reorder_level
//    (inclusive of fully out-of-stock — a broader definition than the
//    "low" KPI on Warehouse Tasks/Stock Adjustments, which excludes
//    out-of-stock; disclosed via the card's own sublabel so the two
//    numbers are never confused), real out-of-stock sub-count. "3
//    restocks due" has no real equivalent (no expected-restock-date field
//    exists) — omitted rather than invented.
//  - "Sales vs target" chart: renamed "Revenue trend" — the dashed
//    "Target" line is fabricated (no sales-target/quota entity exists
//    anywhere in this schema) and is not reproduced at all, not even as a
//    placeholder. The solid line/area is real: actual monthly revenue for
//    the trailing 12 real IST calendar months (zero-filled for months
//    with genuinely no orders — a real, true zero, not an invented one),
//    same dashboard_revenue_trend RPC bucketed by month here instead of
//    by day.
//  - "Support queue": real support_tickets counts by status
//    (support_tickets_select_admin already grants admin unscoped read —
//    same RLS every other admin query on this table relies on).
//    "Resolved this week" is relabeled "Resolved in the last 7 days" (real
//    resolved/closed count with updated_at in that real window, same 7d
//    IST convention as every other dashboard) rather than claiming a
//    literal calendar-week boundary this component doesn't actually
//    compute. The "latest ticket" line shows the real most-recently-
//    updated ticket's real subject (never a fabricated "TK-####" id, same
//    reasoning already established on Inventory Staff's own ticket
//    screens) and its real assignee's real name — admin genuinely can see
//    any profile (profiles_select_all_for_admin), unlike inventory_staff —
//    or an honest "Not yet assigned" when assigned_to is null (which it
//    genuinely is for the current real latest ticket). No link to an
//    "Open queue"/ticket detail — Admin Support Tickets/Ticket Detail
//    aren't built this turn, and linking to a route that doesn't exist
//    yet would be worse than no link.
//  - "Stock alerts" table: same real low/out-of-stock product set as the
//    KPI card above, SKU/name/on-hand/reorder-at/status all real.
//    "Location" column: no warehouse/bin/location field exists anywhere in
//    this schema (same as every other screen's own honest "—" for this
//    exact gap) — column kept (matches the design's grid shape), value
//    honestly "—". "View all"/"Request restock" links omitted — their
//    real destinations (Admin Stock) don't exist yet this turn.
//  - "Sales team vs target": renamed "Sales by team member" — no
//    sales-target/quota entity exists (same reasoning as the chart above).
//    Real data instead: every real sales_staff profile (admin can see all
//    profiles) joined against orders.placed_by (a real column — the
//    sales_staff who placed that order via Sales' own New Order flow),
//    summed to a real per-rep total. Bars are scaled relative to the
//    top-performing real rep this period, not to any target — no
//    percentage-of-target label, since there is no target.
//  - Header "+ New" button, search ("⌘K"), notifications unread dot: see
//    AdminNavTop.astro's own header comment — all either omitted or
//    rendered honestly disabled there.
//  - "Export" button: no export/report-generation capability exists
//    anywhere in this project — omitted.
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NavSidebar from "../../components/staff/NavSidebar.astro";
import AdminNavTop from "../../components/staff/AdminNavTop.astro";
import { resolveDashboardRange, DASHBOARD_RANGE_PRESETS, buildDashboardRangeUrl } from "../../lib/dashboardRange";

// dashboard_revenue_trend's real return shape (day/revenue/order_count) —
// not present in the generated Supabase types (RPC return rows come back
// untyped), so annotated explicitly here to satisfy strict mode.
interface RevenueTrendRow {
  day: string;
  revenue: number;
  order_count: number;
}

const url = Astro.url;
const range = resolveDashboardRange(url.searchParams.get("range"));
const viewerRole = (Astro.locals.role === "super_admin" ? "super_admin" : "admin") as "admin" | "super_admin";

// Same IST-anchoring technique dashboardRange.ts already uses (see that
// file's own header comment), generalized to calendar-month boundaries —
// needed here because dashboardRange.ts only exports fixed day-count/YTD
// presets, not month boundaries.
const IST_OFFSET_MS = 5.5 * 60 * 60 * 1000;
function istMonthBoundsUtc(year: number, month0: number): { from: string; to: string } {
  const fromUtcMs = Date.UTC(year, month0, 1) - IST_OFFSET_MS;
  const toUtcMs = Date.UTC(year, month0 + 1, 1) - IST_OFFSET_MS;
  return { from: new Date(fromUtcMs).toISOString(), to: new Date(toUtcMs).toISOString() };
}
const nowIst = new Date(Date.now() + IST_OFFSET_MS);
const curYear = nowIst.getUTCFullYear();
const curMonth0 = nowIst.getUTCMonth();
const thisMonth = istMonthBoundsUtc(curYear, curMonth0);
const prevMonthRef = new Date(Date.UTC(curYear, curMonth0 - 1, 1));
const prevMonth = istMonthBoundsUtc(prevMonthRef.getUTCFullYear(), prevMonthRef.getUTCMonth());
const twelveMoStart = istMonthBoundsUtc(curYear, curMonth0 - 11).from;
const MONTH_LABELS = ["Jan", "Feb", "Mar", "Apr", "May", "Jun", "Jul", "Aug", "Sep", "Oct", "Nov", "Dec"];

const OPEN_STATUSES = ["pending", "confirmed", "processing", "shipped"] as const;
const LOW_STOCK_WINDOW = resolveDashboardRange("7d");

const [
  { data: mtdRevenueRows },
  { data: prevMonthRevenueRows },
  { data: trend12moRows },
  { data: inventoryValueRow },
  { count: activeProductCount },
  { count: categoryCount },
  { data: inventoryRows },
  { data: openOrderRows },
  { data: salesStaffRows },
  { data: ticketRows },
] = await Promise.all([
  Astro.locals.supabase.rpc("dashboard_revenue_trend", { p_from: thisMonth.from, p_to: thisMonth.to }),
  Astro.locals.supabase.rpc("dashboard_revenue_trend", { p_from: prevMonth.from, p_to: prevMonth.to }),
  Astro.locals.supabase.rpc("dashboard_revenue_trend", { p_from: twelveMoStart, p_to: thisMonth.to }),
  Astro.locals.supabase.from("inventory_value_summary").select("inventory_value").maybeSingle(),
  Astro.locals.supabase.from("products").select("id", { count: "exact", head: true }).eq("is_active", true),
  Astro.locals.supabase.from("categories").select("id", { count: "exact", head: true }),
  Astro.locals.supabase
    .from("products")
    .select("sku, name, inventory(quantity_on_hand, reorder_level)")
    .eq("is_active", true),
  Astro.locals.supabase.from("orders").select("status, total").in("status", OPEN_STATUSES as unknown as string[]),
  Astro.locals.supabase.from("profiles").select("id, full_name").eq("role", "sales_staff"),
  Astro.locals.supabase.from("support_tickets").select("id, subject, status, assigned_to, updated_at").order("updated_at", { ascending: false }),
]);

const formatCurrency = (value: number) =>
  new Intl.NumberFormat("en-IN", { style: "currency", currency: "INR", maximumFractionDigits: 0 }).format(value);

// --- Revenue this month + MoM ---
const mtdRows = (mtdRevenueRows ?? []) as RevenueTrendRow[];
const prevMonthRows = (prevMonthRevenueRows ?? []) as RevenueTrendRow[];
const mtdRevenue = mtdRows.reduce((sum: number, r: RevenueTrendRow) => sum + Number(r.revenue), 0);
const prevMonthRevenue = prevMonthRows.reduce((sum: number, r: RevenueTrendRow) => sum + Number(r.revenue), 0);
const momChangePct = prevMonthRevenue > 0 ? ((mtdRevenue - prevMonthRevenue) / prevMonthRevenue) * 100 : null;
const prevMonthLabel = MONTH_LABELS[prevMonthRef.getUTCMonth()];

// Real per-day sparkline points (only days with real revenue — the RPC
// doesn't zero-fill within a month, same as everywhere else it's used).
const sparkPoints = mtdRows.map((r: RevenueTrendRow) => Number(r.revenue));
const sparkMax = Math.max(...sparkPoints, 1);
const sparkSvgPoints = sparkPoints
  .map((v: number, i: number) => {
    const x = sparkPoints.length > 1 ? (i / (sparkPoints.length - 1)) * 96 : 0;
    const y = 34 - (v / sparkMax) * 32;
    return `${x.toFixed(1)},${y.toFixed(1)}`;
  })
  .join(" ");

// --- Open orders ---
const openOrders = openOrderRows ?? [];
const openOrdersValue = openOrders.reduce((sum, r) => sum + Number(r.total), 0);
const openByStatus = new Map<string, number>();
for (const r of openOrders) openByStatus.set(r.status, (openByStatus.get(r.status) ?? 0) + 1);
const OPEN_STATUS_LABEL: Record<string, string> = { pending: "pending", confirmed: "confirmed", processing: "processing", shipped: "shipped" };
const openBreakdown = OPEN_STATUSES.filter((s) => (openByStatus.get(s) ?? 0) > 0)
  .map((s) => `${openByStatus.get(s)} ${OPEN_STATUS_LABEL[s]}`)
  .join(" · ");

// --- Inventory value + low stock ---
const inventoryValue = Number(inventoryValueRow?.inventory_value ?? 0);
function inventoryOf(row: { inventory: unknown }): { quantity_on_hand: number; reorder_level: number } | null {
  const inv = row.inventory as unknown as { quantity_on_hand: number; reorder_level: number }[] | null;
  return inv?.[0] ?? null;
}
const stockRows = (inventoryRows ?? []).map((p) => {
  const inv = inventoryOf(p);
  return { sku: p.sku as string, name: p.name as string, qty: inv?.quantity_on_hand ?? 0, reorder: inv?.reorder_level ?? 0 };
});
const alertRows = stockRows
  .filter((r) => r.qty <= r.reorder)
  .sort((a, b) => a.qty - b.qty)
  .slice(0, 8);
const outOfStockCount = stockRows.filter((r) => r.qty === 0).length;
const lowStockCount = stockRows.filter((r) => r.qty <= r.reorder).length;

// --- Revenue trend, 12 real calendar months (zero-filled — a real zero
// for a month with genuinely no orders, not an invented number) ---
const revenueByMonth = new Map<string, number>();
for (const r of trend12moRows ?? []) {
  const ym = String(r.day).slice(0, 7);
  revenueByMonth.set(ym, (revenueByMonth.get(ym) ?? 0) + Number(r.revenue));
}
const trendMonths = Array.from({ length: 12 }, (_, i) => {
  const d = new Date(Date.UTC(curYear, curMonth0 - 11 + i, 1));
  const ym = `${d.getUTCFullYear()}-${String(d.getUTCMonth() + 1).padStart(2, "0")}`;
  return { label: MONTH_LABELS[d.getUTCMonth()], value: revenueByMonth.get(ym) ?? 0 };
});
const trendMax = Math.max(...trendMonths.map((m) => m.value), 1);
const CHART_W = 700;
const CHART_H = 190;
const CHART_X_MARGIN = 40;
// Extra right-side room so the last month's center-anchored label doesn't
// clip against the viewBox edge (the last data point sits exactly at
// CHART_X_MARGIN + CHART_W).
const CHART_X_RIGHT_PAD = 24;
// x/y already include the left axis-label margin, so the SVG markup below
// can use these points directly with no further offset math.
const trendLinePoints = trendMonths.map((m, i) => ({
  x: CHART_X_MARGIN + (i / (trendMonths.length - 1)) * CHART_W,
  y: CHART_H - (m.value / trendMax) * CHART_H,
}));
const trendAreaPath =
  `M ${trendLinePoints.map((p) => `${p.x.toFixed(1)},${p.y.toFixed(1)}`).join(" L ")}` +
  ` L ${(CHART_W + CHART_X_MARGIN).toFixed(1)},${CHART_H} L ${CHART_X_MARGIN},${CHART_H} Z`;
const latestTrendMonth = trendMonths[trendMonths.length - 1];

// --- Support queue ---
const tickets = ticketRows ?? [];
const ticketCounts = { open: 0, in_progress: 0, waiting: 0 };
for (const t of tickets) {
  if (t.status === "open") ticketCounts.open++;
  else if (t.status === "in_progress") ticketCounts.in_progress++;
  else if (t.status === "waiting") ticketCounts.waiting++;
}
const activeTicketCount = ticketCounts.open + ticketCounts.in_progress + ticketCounts.waiting;
const resolvedRecentCount = tickets.filter(
  (t) =>
    (t.status === "resolved" || t.status === "closed") &&
    LOW_STOCK_WINDOW.from &&
    (t.updated_at as string) >= LOW_STOCK_WINDOW.from
).length;
const queueRows = [
  { label: "Open", n: ticketCounts.open },
  { label: "In progress", n: ticketCounts.in_progress },
  { label: "Waiting", n: ticketCounts.waiting },
];
const queueMax = Math.max(...queueRows.map((r) => r.n), 1);

const latestTicket = tickets[0] ?? null;
let latestTicketAssigneeName: string | null = null;
if (latestTicket?.assigned_to) {
  const { data: assigneeProfile } = await Astro.locals.supabase
    .from("profiles")
    .select("full_name")
    .eq("id", latestTicket.assigned_to)
    .maybeSingle();
  latestTicketAssigneeName = assigneeProfile?.full_name ?? null;
}

// --- Sales by team member (real orders.placed_by attribution, no target) ---
const { data: repOrderRows } = await Astro.locals.supabase.from("orders").select("placed_by, total").not("placed_by", "is", null);
const repTotals = new Map<string, number>();
for (const r of repOrderRows ?? []) {
  const id = r.placed_by as string;
  repTotals.set(id, (repTotals.get(id) ?? 0) + Number(r.total));
}
const reps = (salesStaffRows ?? [])
  .map((s) => ({ id: s.id as string, name: (s.full_name as string) || "—", amount: repTotals.get(s.id as string) ?? 0 }))
  .sort((a, b) => b.amount - a.amount);
const repMax = Math.max(...reps.map((r) => r.amount), 1);

const currentMonthLabel = new Date(thisMonth.from).toLocaleDateString("en-IN", { month: "long", year: "numeric", timeZone: "Asia/Kolkata" });
---

<BaseLayout title="Business overview — Admin">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="sd" id="sd-root">
    <div id="sd-sidebar-backdrop" class="sd__backdrop"></div>

    <div id="sd-sidebar" class="sd__sidebar">
      <NavSidebar active="Dashboard" role="admin" viewerRole={viewerRole} />
    </div>

    <div class="sd__panel">
      <AdminNavTop section="Dashboard" page="Overview" />

      <main id="main-content" class="ad__main">
        <div class="ad__header">
          <div class="ad__heading-col">
            <h1>Business overview</h1>
            <span class="ad__subtitle">Store-wide · {currentMonthLabel}</span>
          </div>
          <div role="group" aria-label="Period" class="ad__period">
            {DASHBOARD_RANGE_PRESETS.map((p) => (
              <a href={buildDashboardRangeUrl(url, "/admin", p.value)} class={`ad__period-btn ${range.preset === p.value ? "is-active" : ""}`}>
                {p.label}
              </a>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ad__kpis">
          <div class="ad__kpi-card">
            <span class="ad__kpi-label">Revenue this month</span>
            <div class="ad__kpi-row">
              <div class="ad__kpi-col">
                <span class="ad__kpi-value">{formatCurrency(mtdRevenue)}</span>
                <span class="ad__kpi-note">
                  {momChangePct !== null ? (
                    <Fragment>
                      <span class={momChangePct >= 0 ? "ad__delta-up" : "ad__delta-down"}>
                        {momChangePct >= 0 ? "▲" : "▼"} {Math.abs(momChangePct).toFixed(1)}%
                      </span>{" "}
                      vs {prevMonthLabel}
                    </Fragment>
                  ) : (
                    `No orders in ${prevMonthLabel}`
                  )}
                </span>
              </div>
              {sparkPoints.length > 1 && (
                <svg width="96" height="36" viewBox="0 0 96 36" aria-hidden="true" class="ad__sparkline">
                  <polyline points={sparkSvgPoints} fill="none" stroke="var(--sd-accent)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
                </svg>
              )}
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="ad__kpi-card">
            <span class="ad__kpi-label">Open orders</span>
            <div class="ad__kpi-row">
              <div class="ad__kpi-col">
                <span class="ad__kpi-value">{openOrders.length} order{openOrders.length === 1 ? "" : "s"}</span>
                <span class="ad__kpi-note">{formatCurrency(openOrdersValue)}{openBreakdown ? ` · ${openBreakdown}` : ""}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="ad__kpi-card">
            <span class="ad__kpi-label">Inventory value</span>
            <div class="ad__kpi-row">
              <div class="ad__kpi-col">
                <span class="ad__kpi-value">{formatCurrency(inventoryValue)}</span>
                <span class="ad__kpi-note">{activeProductCount ?? 0} SKUs · {categoryCount ?? 0} categories</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="ad__kpi-card">
            <div class="ad__kpi-top">
              <span class="ad__kpi-label">Stock needing attention</span>
              {lowStockCount > 0 && <span class="ad__needs-action">Needs action</span>}
            </div>
            <div class="ad__kpi-col">
              <span class="ad__kpi-value">{lowStockCount}</span>
              <span class="ad__kpi-note">{outOfStockCount} out of stock · {lowStockCount - outOfStockCount} low</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ad__charts">
          <section class="ad__chart-card">
            <div class="ad__section-head">
              <div class="ad__section-head-col">
                <h2>Revenue trend</h2>
                <span class="ad__section-sub">Last 12 months · real orders, cancelled excluded</span>
              </div>
              <span class="ad__legend"><span class="ad__legend-swatch"></span>Revenue</span>
            </div>
            <svg width="100%" height="222" viewBox={`0 0 ${CHART_W + CHART_X_MARGIN + CHART_X_RIGHT_PAD} 222`} role="img" aria-label={`Revenue by month, last 12 months, latest ${latestTrendMonth.label} ${formatCurrency(latestTrendMonth.value)}`} class="ad__trend-svg">
              <g stroke="var(--sd-border)" stroke-width="1">
                <path d={`M40 10H${CHART_W + 40}M40 55H${CHART_W + 40}M40 100H${CHART_W + 40}M40 145H${CHART_W + 40}`} />
              </g>
              <path d={`M40 ${CHART_H}H${CHART_W + 40}`} stroke="var(--sd-input)" stroke-width="1" />
              <path d={trendAreaPath} fill="var(--sd-accent)" fill-opacity="0.1" />
              <polyline points={trendLinePoints.map((p) => `${p.x.toFixed(1)},${p.y.toFixed(1)}`).join(" ")} fill="none" stroke="var(--sd-accent)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" />
              {trendLinePoints.map((p, i) => (
                <text x={p.x} y="212" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--sd-muted-fg)">{trendMonths[i].label}</text>
              ))}
            </svg>
          </section>

          <section class="ad__side-card">
            <div class="ad__section-head">
              <div class="ad__section-head-col">
                <h2>Support queue</h2>
                <span class="ad__section-sub">{activeTicketCount} active ticket{activeTicketCount === 1 ? "" : "s"} · by status</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="ad__queue">
              {queueRows.map((r) => (
                <div class="ad__queue-row">
                  <div class="ad__queue-row-top">
                    <span>{r.label}</span>
                    <span><span class="ad__queue-n">{r.n}</span> <span class="ad__queue-unit">{r.n === 1 ? "ticket" : "tickets"}</span></span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="ad__queue-bar-track"><div class="ad__queue-bar" style={`width:${(r.n / queueMax) * 100}%`}></div></div>
                </div>
              ))}
              <div class="ad__queue-row">
                <div class="ad__queue-row-top">
                  <span>Resolved (last 7 days)</span>
                  <span><span class="ad__queue-n">{resolvedRecentCount}</span></span>
                </div>
                <div class="ad__queue-bar-track"><div class="ad__queue-bar ad__queue-bar--resolved" style={`width:${Math.min(100, (resolvedRecentCount / queueMax) * 100)}%`}></div></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="ad__spacer" />
            {latestTicket && (
              <div class="ad__latest-ticket">
                <span class="ad__latest-dot" />
                <span class="ad__latest-text">
                  <strong>{latestTicket.subject}</strong>{" "}
                  {latestTicketAssigneeName ? `assigned to ${latestTicketAssigneeName}` : "not yet assigned"}
                </span>
                <span class="ad__latest-date">{new Date(latestTicket.updated_at as string).toLocaleDateString("en-IN", { day: "numeric", month: "short" })}</span>
              </div>
            )}
          </section>
        </div>

        <div class="ad__bottom">
          <section class="ad__stock-card">
            <div class="ad__section-head ad__section-head--padded">
              <h2>Stock alerts</h2>
              <span class="ad__section-sub">{lowStockCount} product{lowStockCount === 1 ? "" : "s"} at or below reorder level</span>
            </div>
            {
              alertRows.length > 0 ? (
                <Fragment>
                  <div class="ad__stock-grid ad__stock-grid--head">
                    <span>SKU</span><span>Product</span><span>Location</span><span class="ad__col-right">On hand</span><span class="ad__col-right">Reorder at</span><span>Status</span>
                  </div>
                  {alertRows.map((a) => (
                    <div class="ad__stock-grid ad__stock-row">
                      <span class="ad__stock-sku">{a.sku}</span>
                      <span class="ad__stock-name">{a.name}</span>
                      <span class="ad__stock-loc">—</span>
                      <span class="ad__col-right ad__stock-qty">{a.qty}</span>
                      <span class="ad__col-right ad__stock-reorder">{a.reorder}</span>
                      <span><span class={`ad__stock-pill ${a.qty === 0 ? "ad__stock-pill--out" : "ad__stock-pill--low"}`}>{a.qty === 0 ? "Out" : "Low"}</span></span>
                    </div>
                  ))}
                </Fragment>
              ) : (
                <p class="ad__empty">No products at or below their reorder level.</p>
              )
            }
          </section>

          <section class="ad__reps-card">
            <div class="ad__section-head">
              <h2>Sales by team member</h2>
              <span class="ad__section-sub">{currentMonthLabel.split(" ")[0]} · lifetime</span>
            </div>
            {
              reps.length > 0 ? (
                reps.map((r) => (
                  <div class="ad__rep-row">
                    <div class="ad__rep-avatar">{r.name.split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean).slice(0, 2).map((p) => p[0]?.toUpperCase()).join("") || "?"}</div>
                    <div class="ad__rep-col">
                      <div class="ad__rep-top">
                        <span class="ad__rep-name">{r.name}</span>
                        <span class="ad__rep-amount">{formatCurrency(r.amount)}</span>
                      </div>
                      <div class="ad__rep-bar-track"><div class="ad__rep-bar" style={`width:${(r.amount / repMax) * 100}%`}></div></div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                ))
              ) : (
                <p class="ad__empty">No sales staff yet.</p>
              )
            }
          </section>
        </div>
      </main>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

